  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contracting in Wisconsin reached $2.9B in obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 51,145 awards with an average award size of $56.3K. Obligations fell 54.1% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $2B, making it the largest buying agency in the state for the period. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. received $1.9B in obligations and is the largest vendor. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) is the largest industry by obligations at $1.8B. Other notable buyers include the Department of Defense with $457M and the Department of Agriculture with $169M. Other notable vendors include OSHKOSH DEFENSE LLC with $455M and AMTEC CORPORATION with $267M. Historical annual obligations show variation across fiscal years: FY21 $5.8B, FY22 $5.2B, FY23 $5.3B, FY24 $8.9B, FY25 $6.3B, and FY26 $2.9B. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 contracting compare to prior years?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations are $2.9B, down 54.1% year over year. Fiscal year obligations before FY26 were FY25 $6.3B, FY24 $8.9B, FY23 $5.3B, FY22 $5.2B, and FY21 $5.8B. The year-to-date total reflects partial fiscal year reporting."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and vendors in Wisconsin this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer with $2B in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $457M and the Department of Agriculture with $169M. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. is the largest vendor with $1.9B, followed by OSHKOSH DEFENSE LLC with $455M and AMTEC CORPORATION with $267M. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) is the top industry at $1.8B."
      }
    ]
  },
